\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Inversion and charge conjugation of the grading}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{For the \vocabk{covariant centered differences}{fdip-009O}
on the Pauli module of \ref{fdip-00LB}, every dimension #{n\ge1}
admits antiunitaries #{c_\pm} with
#{c_\pm^2=\bbI} and
#{c_\pm\varepsilon_j^Sc_\pm^{-1}=\pm\varepsilon_j^S}.
At spacing #{a>0} take the centered operator #{D_{a,U}},
the Laplacian with #{-L_{a,U}\ge0}, and the
\vocabk{Wilson operator}{fdip-009U}
#{D_{W,a,U}=D_{a,U}-c_WL_{a,U}}.
For any antiunitary #{c_F} on the fiber, put
#{\mathcal Q=c_\pm\otimes c_F} sitewise and
#{U^{\mathcal Q}=c_F U c_F^{-1}} on the represented links. Then
##{\begin{aligned}
\mathcal Q D_{a,U}\mathcal Q^{-1}&=\pm D_{a,U^{\mathcal Q}},\\
\mathcal Q L_{a,U}\mathcal Q^{-1}&=L_{a,U^{\mathcal Q}}.
\end{aligned}}
In dimension #{n=2m} both maps take the volume grading #{C} of
\ref{fdip-009X} to #{(-1)^m C}.}

\p{For #{n\ge1} and any Hermitian Euclidean Clifford module,
#{\mathcal P=(\varepsilon_1^S\otimes\bbI_F)h^*}, with
#{h(x)=(x_1,-x_2,\ldots,-x_n)}, carries the centered, Laplace
and Wilson operators to those for #{U^{\mathcal P}}. Here #{h^*} denotes pullback.
#{\mathcal P} negates any site-independent complex-linear self-adjoint
\vocabk{grading}{fdip-013N}
#{\Gamma} on #{S\otimes F} anticommuting with
#{\varepsilon_1^S\otimes\bbI_F}, including #{C} for even #{n}.
On transported #{\Gamma}-stable kernels and generalized kernels,
#{\mathcal P} reverses the index. For #{n=2m} on Pauli spin,
#{\mathcal Q} multiplies the transported #{C}-index by #{(-1)^m}.}

\proof{
\p{Let #{c_+} conjugate the coefficients in the product basis
of \ref{fdip-00LB}. It is antiunitary of square #{\bbI} and commutes with the real
generators. For the sign
array #{Z} put #{c_-=Z^{\otimes n}c_+}. The real unitary
#{Z^{\otimes n}} commutes with #{c_+} and squares to #{\bbI}, so
#{c_-} is antiunitary of square #{\bbI}. Conjugating by
#{Z} negates the single flip in each generator, giving the minus branch. Since the
generators are real symmetric, #{C_\gamma=Z^{\otimes n}} and
#{\gamma_\mu=\varepsilon_\mu^S} satisfy
##{C_\gamma\gamma_\mu C_\gamma^{-1}=-\gamma_\mu^T,}
the transpose relation in
\citet{Eq. (2.4), p. 2}{igarashi2009cp}, here realized by the matrix factor of #{c_-}.}

\p{The rule #{s\otimes v\mapsto c_\pm(s)\otimes c_F(v)}
conjugates a scalar on either factor, so it defines an antiunitary
with square #{\bbI_S\otimes c_F^2}. The new links belong to the
conjugated representation #{g\mapsto c_F\rho(g)c_F^{-1}} and
remain in the original represented group if #{c_F} normalizes it.
The shift formulas of the [covariant centered differences](fdip-009O)
conjugate link transports and their inverses. The coefficients of
the differences and Laplacian are real, giving the stated operator
identities. When #{n=2m}, the product #{P=\psI} of all generators
is fixed by either sign. Conjugating the scalar in #{C=\ui^m P}
gives #{(-\ui)^m=(-1)^m\ui^m}.}

\p{Write #{h(x)=(x_1,-x_2,\ldots,-x_n)} and let
#{e_j} be the positive unit step in site direction #{j}. The
[source-to-head convention](fdip-006D) gives
##{\begin{aligned}
U^{\mathcal P}_1(x)&=U_1(hx),\\
U^{\mathcal P}_j(x)&=U_j(hx-e_j)^{-1}
\quad(j>1).
\end{aligned}}
Pullback by #{h} preserves the forward shift in direction one,
with reflected links. For #{j>1} it gives the backward value at
#{x-e_j} multiplied by #{U_j(hx)^{-1}}, precisely
#{U_j^{\mathcal P}(x-e_j)}. Each reflected difference
therefore changes sign. Conjugation by #{\varepsilon_1^S}
reverses exactly the corresponding generators, and exchanging
shifts preserves their sum in the Laplacian. Hence
##{\begin{aligned}
\mathcal P D_{a,U}\mathcal P^{-1}&=D_{a,U^{\mathcal P}},\\
\mathcal P L_{a,U}\mathcal P^{-1}&=L_{a,U^{\mathcal P}}.
\end{aligned}}
Their Wilson combination transforms with them.}

\p{Pullback commutes with the constant #{\Gamma}, and the first
generator exchanges its eigenspaces. Hence
#{\mathcal P\Gamma\mathcal P^{-1}=-\Gamma}.
Charge conjugation preserves or exchanges the #{C}-eigenspaces
according to #{(-1)^m}. Both maps preserve complex dimension.
Intertwining #{A_U\mapsto\pm A_{U'}} transports kernels of all
powers. Subtracting the eigenspace dimensions gives the index signs.
If #{U^{\mathcal P}=U}, a #{\Gamma}-stable centered kernel is
#{\mathcal P}-invariant and has index zero.}
}
